{
  "paraId": "4CA1EE50",
  "style": "",
  "text": "Nowadays, managing colorectal liver metastasis involves the multidisciplinary approach including surgery 24. Our results compare favorably with previous reports. Median OS was longer with HAIC after both systemic oxaliplatin- and irinotecan-based chemotherapy (HAIC-FOLFOX-B: median 12.9 months; HAIC-FOLFIRI-B: median, 17.4 months) than with other third-line chemotherapies (regorafenib: median, 6.4 months; TAS-102: median, 9.0 months) 10, 11. In patients refractory to standard chemotherapy, HAIC-FOLFOX-B and HAIC-FOLFIRI-B were effective, with disease control rates of 70.0% and 86.3%, respectively (Table 2). HAIC also has low systemic toxicity, with adverse effects less frequent than previously reported (Table 3), and is better tolerated than systemic chemotherapy, especially by frail patients after multiple prior regimens."
}

