  "text": "Notably, HAIC, using the same drugs that became ineffective through systemic administration, was effective in this study. Some reports have shown that HAIC using the same drugs was effective in patients with systemic chemotherapy-resistant CRC 27, 28 . We reported a similar phenomenon in intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma 22. Although the mechanism of this phenomenon is unclear, we present an explanation for the effectiveness of high concentrations of anticancer agents in the liver against resistant tumor cells. Additionally, small amounts of the drug might enter non-tumor tissues throughout the body and reduce drug distribution in organs other than the liver 29. Although these treatments are suitable only for managing patients with liver metastases, they have high disease control rates and consequent survival benefits."
