  "text": "The results of the present study indicated that HAIC-FOLFOX-B and HAIC-FOLFIRI-B were effective in patients who received previous systemic chemotherapy and had been refractory to it, which is in line with previous reports showing that HAIC remains active against chemotherapy-resistant colorectal liver metastases 27, 28. The response rates (25.0% and 4.5%) and median OS (12.9 and 17.4 months) observed here are also comparable to, or better than, those of the previous HAIC plus systemic chemotherapy series listed in Table 4, including the 21.3% response rate and 8.3-month median OS reported for third- or fourth-line patients by Lim et al. 39 These treatments had a high disease control rate and consequent survival benefits in patients who had undergone previous chemotherapy."
